{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"extension","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cliques"}],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P7CliquesE07maximalC0AD07MaximalC0VyxGyF","title":"Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/coreNumbers()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount()","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/cliqueNumber()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cliqueNumber()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cliqueNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"role":"symbol","title":"cliqueNumber()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The size of a largest clique of the simple graph, ω: 0 for the empty graph, 1 for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edgeless one, at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracy + 1"},{"type":"text","text":". Branch and bound in degeneracy order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex’s later neighbors (at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degeneracy"},{"type":"text","text":", those with a high enough core number)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the candidates, one search per vertex that raises the best size as it goes, stopping at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the degeneracy bound. Each search is San Segundo et al.’s BBMC on bitsets, candidates in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"descending degree, branching from the highest greedy colour down. Exponential in the worst"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"case; memory O(n + m + degeneracy²)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/cliquenumber()","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficients()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficients()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clusteringCoefficients","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ClusteringCoefficients","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques22ClusteringCoefficientsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficients()","title":"clusteringCoefficients()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Triangles and clustering for every vertex of the simple graph (self-loops ignored,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parallel edges counted once), in one compact-forward pass. O(m^(3\/2)).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"triangleCount"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount()","title":"triangleCount()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The number of triangles in the simple graph. O(m^(3\/2)).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/averageClustering()":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/averageclustering()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"averageClustering"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"title":"averageClustering()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/averageClustering()","abstract":[{"text":"The mean local clustering coefficient over every vertex, zeros included, summed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; 0 when empty.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstmaximumclique()","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first largest clique: of all the largest cliques, the least by vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and parallel edges are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored. Of two cliques of one size, the lesser is the one holding the least vertex of their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symmetric difference. After "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cliqueNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s search, each largest clique is searched for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its first vertex v in degeneracy order, among v’s later neighbors, so memory stays O(n +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"m + degeneracy²) however large a hub’s degree. For each v, a witness clique W (any one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right size) guides a pass over the candidates in ascending number: a candidate in W is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taken, any other is taken exactly when a search finds the rest of a clique among the common"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbors left (which then becomes W). A v whose candidates all exceed the least vertex of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the best clique so far is skipped. Up to one search per vertex and candidate, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exponential in the worst case, so it can be far slower than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":"; the search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not check for task cancellation."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalCliques()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","text":"MaximalCliques"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","title":"maximalCliques()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; see "},{"code":"MaximalCliques","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored, and an isolated vertex is a clique of one."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques()","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/coreNumbers()":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/corenumbers()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"coreNumbers"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"text":"CoreNumbers","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques11CoreNumbersV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"coreNumbers()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/coreNumbers()","abstract":[{"text":"The core decomposition of the simple graph underlying this one (self-loops ignored,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parallel edges counted once), by Batagelj–Zaversnik’s bucket algorithm. O(n + m).","type":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumClique()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumClique()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumclique()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumClique"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"title":"maximumClique()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A largest clique of the simple graph, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored. Deterministic, but which largest clique it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depends on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It is the clique "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cliqueNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s search finds, so it costs the same: exponential in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worst case, memory O(n + m + degeneracy²). The search does not check for task cancellation."}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/triangleCount(of:)":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/triangleCount(of:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of triangles through "},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", from its neighborhood alone."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/trianglecount(of:)","title":"triangleCount(of:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"triangleCount"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques","kind":"symbol","title":"Cliques","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/clusteringCoefficient(of:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/clusteringCoefficient(of:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/clusteringcoefficient(of:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clusteringCoefficient"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"title":"clusteringCoefficient(of:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local clustering coefficient of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", from its neighborhood alone: 2T \/ (d(d − 1)),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 when it has fewer than two distinct neighbors."}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols/Graph/transitivity()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/transitivity()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transitivity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/transitivity()","title":"transitivity()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Three times the triangles over the connected triples; 0 when there are no triangles.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}